A service can call another service using `RestTemplate` (or `WebClient`).

```java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    private final RestTemplate restTemplate;

    public OrderService(RestTemplate restTemplate) {
        this.restTemplate = restTemplate;
    }

    public User getUser(Long userId) {
        String url = "http://user-service/users/" + userId;
        return restTemplate.getForObject(url, User.class);
    }
}
```

**Problem:** The URL `http://user-service` is hard‑coded. In a dynamic environment, we need service discovery.

Spring Cloud Feign makes HTTP clients declarative:

```java
@FeignClient(name = "user-service")
public interface UserClient {
    @GetMapping("/users/{id}")
    User getUser(@PathVariable("id") Long id);
}
```

Then inject `UserClient` and call it like a local method. Feign integrates with service discovery automatically.

You'll need to add `@EnableFeignClients` in your main class.
